{"id":"1-corinthians","links":[{"id":"q2","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":11,"v":7},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":1,"v":26},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians calls man “the image and glory of God”; in Genesis, God says, “Let Us make man in Our image.”"},{"id":"q3","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":49},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":1,"v":26},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians speaks of bearing “the likeness of the earthly man”; in Genesis, God says, “Let Us make man in Our image, after Our likeness.”"},{"id":"q12","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":45},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":2,"v":7},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “became a living being” from Genesis, where the LORD God forms man from the dust and breathes life into him."},{"id":"q13","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":47},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":2,"v":7},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says the first man “was of the dust of the earth”; Genesis says God formed man “from the dust of the ground.”"},{"id":"q16","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":6,"v":16},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":2,"v":24},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “will become one flesh” from Genesis, and uses it to speak of a man united with a prostitute."},{"id":"q17","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":6,"v":17},"b":{"book":"genesis","c":2,"v":24},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says one united with the Lord “is one with Him in spirit”; Genesis says a man united to his wife becomes one flesh."},{"id":"q141","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":7},"b":{"book":"exodus","c":32,"v":6},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats that the people “sat down to eat and drink” and “got up to indulge in revelry”; Exodus says the same after offerings."},{"id":"q168","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":5},"b":{"book":"numbers","c":14,"v":16},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says most “were struck down in the wilderness”; Numbers has this saying about the LORD: “He has slaughtered them in the wilderness.”"},{"id":"q214","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":5,"v":13},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":17,"v":7},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says, “Expel the wicked man from among you”; Deuteronomy says, “you must purge the evil from among you.”"},{"id":"q231","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":9,"v":9},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":25,"v":4},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain”; the same words stand in Deuteronomy."},{"id":"q243","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":20},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":32,"v":17},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “to demons, not to God” for pagan sacrifices; Deuteronomy says “They sacrificed to demons, not to God.”"},{"id":"q245","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":22},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":32,"v":21},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians asks “Are we trying to provoke the Lord to jealousy?”; Deuteronomy says “They have provoked My jealousy.”"},{"id":"q271","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":3,"v":19},"b":{"book":"job","c":5,"v":13},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “He catches the wise in their craftiness”; the same words stand in the book of Job."},{"id":"q296","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":27},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":8,"v":6},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says “God has put everything under His feet”; Psalms says “You have placed everything under his feet.”"},{"id":"q319","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":26},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":24,"v":1},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness thereof”; Psalms 24:1 has the same words."},{"id":"q372","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":3,"v":20},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":94,"v":11},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians quotes Psalms, but writes “the thoughts of the wise” where Psalms has “the thoughts of man”."},{"id":"q406","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":25},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":110,"v":1},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says He must reign until His enemies are “under His feet”; Psalms says “a footstool for Your feet”."},{"id":"q505","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":32},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":22,"v":13},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats Isaiah: “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die”."},{"id":"q508","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":54},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":25,"v":8},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says “Death has been swallowed up in victory”; Isaiah says “He will swallow up death forever”."},{"id":"q512","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":14,"v":21},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":28,"v":11},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians has “foreign lips I will speak to this people”; Isaiah has “foreign tongues, He will speak to this people”."},{"id":"q513","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":14,"v":21},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":28,"v":12},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says “they will not listen to Me”; Isaiah says “But they would not listen”."},{"id":"q523","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":1,"v":19},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":29,"v":14},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats Isaiah: “the wisdom of the wise” and “the intelligence of the intelligent”, with “I will destroy” where Isaiah says “will vanish”."},{"id":"q541","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":2,"v":16},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":40,"v":13},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians asks “who has known the mind of the Lord”; Isaiah asks “Who has directed the Spirit of the LORD”."},{"id":"q574","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":2,"v":9},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":52,"v":15},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says no eye has seen and no ear has heard; Isaiah says kings “will understand what they have not heard.”"},{"id":"q607","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":2,"v":9},"b":{"book":"isaiah","c":64,"v":4},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats “no eye has seen” from Isaiah, and both passages speak of God acting for those who love or wait for Him."},{"id":"q618","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":2,"v":9},"b":{"book":"jeremiah","c":3,"v":16},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says “no heart has imagined” what God prepared; Jeremiah says the ark of the covenant “will never come to mind.”"},{"id":"q624","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":1,"v":31},"b":{"book":"jeremiah","c":9,"v":24},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats Jeremiah’s call to boast: “him who boasts boast in” the Lord; Jeremiah says to boast that he “understands and knows Me.”"},{"id":"q672","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":15,"v":55},"b":{"book":"hosea","c":13,"v":14},"upstream":["bible-researcher.com","kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians repeats Hosea’s taunt “Where, O Death,” and asks about “your sting”; Hosea also asks about “your plagues.”"},{"id":"q757","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":26},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":10,"v":14},"upstream":["kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians says “The earth is the Lord’s”; Deuteronomy says “the earth and everything in it” belong to the LORD your God."},{"id":"q758","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":28},"b":{"book":"psalms","c":24,"v":1},"upstream":["kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians 10:28 speaks of food “offered to idols”; Psalms says “The earth is the LORD’s, and the fullness thereof”."},{"id":"q759","type":"quotation","source":"Bible Quotation Database","a":{"book":"1-corinthians","c":10,"v":28},"b":{"book":"deuteronomy","c":10,"v":14},"upstream":["kalvesmaki.com"],"reason":"1 Corinthians speaks of food “offered to idols”; Deuteronomy 10:14 sa